Add CORS rules to an Object Storage bucket with the S3 protocol.

USAGE:
  scw object bucket-cors create <bucket ...> [arg=value ...]

ARGS:
  bucket                The name of the bucket
  cors-configuration    The path to the local JSON file containing the CORS configuration.
  [s3-endpoint]         Custom S3 endpoint to use instead of the default
  [s3-use-path-style]   Whether to use path style addressing for S3 API calls or not
  [project-id]          Project ID to use. If none is passed the default project ID will be used
  [region=fr-snc]       Region to target. If none is passed will use default region from the config

FLAGS:
  -h, --help                help for create
      --list-sub-commands   List all subcommands

GLOBAL FLAGS:
  -c, --config string    The path to the config file
  -D, --debug            Enable debug mode
  -o, --output string    Output format: json or human, see 'scw help output' for more info (default "human")
  -p, --profile string   The config profile to use
